abstract: >-
  Offline, standard-library-only Python workbench for explainable OES-512
  replay triage (fixed block score 0.45 max|x| + 0.35 RMS + 0.20 mean|x|,
  flagged when >= a preregistered threshold, with a per-block max-abs
  baseline), a separate OES32 adaptive-tau stream model and 32-value residual
  check, offline outage-snapshot classification, metadata-only failure-capsule
  validation, and a loopback-only local web interface. Version 0.1.0 adds
  hardening fixes with regression tests, a preregistered synthetic stress
  evaluation with a held-out split and calibration split (honest negative
  result: the block score does not beat the max-abs baseline), and a single
  module in which one exact statevector core powers four toy "AI ∩ quantum"
  applications (quantum-kernel classification, QAOA MaxCut, circuit
  compilation with unitary verification, and H2 VQE). Synthetic data only;
  exact classical simulation, not QPU execution or evidence of quantum
  advantage, and not an operational system.
